# Paths declared to contain ONLY fabricated data.
#
# The pre-commit guard relaxes its CONTENT checks (long digit runs, profile
# names) for files under these prefixes. It never relaxes the path check: a file
# inside the real vault is refused regardless of what is listed here.
#
# This file is deliberately a committed artefact rather than a hardcoded list,
# so that widening the exemption shows up in a diff and gets reviewed. Adding a
# line here is a claim you are making on the record: "everything under this path
# is invented."
#
# Luhn-valid SA ID numbers are blocked EVERYWHERE, including here — a checksum-
# valid ID inside a file you called fake is far more likely to be a mistake than
# a coincidence.

vault.example/
tools/py/tests/
tools/scripts/make_fixtures.py
.claude/commands/selftest.md
.claude/hooks/
docs/
